WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.219
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:09.489 --> 00:10.741
This is ruined.

3
00:10.949 --> 00:13.118
I'm doomed.

4
00:13.201 --> 00:14.661
It's all messed up.

5
00:15.537 --> 00:17.789
I have no hope.

6
00:17.873 --> 00:19.291
Gosh.

7
00:19.583 --> 00:21.668
What are we going to do about this?

8
00:21.752 --> 00:24.087
What am I going to do now?

9
00:25.756 --> 00:27.007
Gong Yeon-su.

10
00:30.052 --> 00:33.930
I worked hard on it but it didn't ferment.

11
00:35.974 --> 00:38.644
- Gosh. Too bitter. - What now?

12
00:38.727 --> 00:40.562
- What do you mean? - Over one mistake...

13
00:41.480 --> 00:44.107
Just because it's not fermented properly

14
00:44.191 --> 00:45.567
are you throwing all this out?

15
00:45.984 --> 00:48.654
I wish I could save it too.

16
00:49.112 --> 00:50.489
Do you know how much these beans cost?

17
00:52.366 --> 00:54.493
How can I be saved

18
00:54.576 --> 00:56.411
when not even cheonggukjang can be saved?

19
00:58.622 --> 00:59.831
Find someone else

20
01:00.082 --> 01:01.958
who has a good understanding of our company.

21
01:03.210 --> 01:05.420
I almost threw this at you.

22
01:05.504 --> 01:06.755
She was my blind date.

23
01:06.838 --> 01:09.216
So what? Since when did you care about your blind date?

24
01:09.299 --> 01:10.967
She threw up on my clothes in the club.

25
01:11.051 --> 01:12.803
People make mistakes.

26
01:12.886 --> 01:14.137
It's actually better this way.

27
01:14.221 --> 01:16.014
It was rather a sophisticated meeting.

28
01:16.556 --> 01:18.183
- Sophisticated? - Yes.

29
01:19.685 --> 01:22.145
They're mine. Perfect. I love it.

30
01:26.441 --> 01:27.442
Drink.

31
01:33.281 --> 01:34.616
This isn't right.

32
01:34.700 --> 01:36.368
I'm sorry, Se-ra. I can't do it.

33
01:36.451 --> 01:39.121
You can't back out now. You said you'd give it a shot.

34
01:39.204 --> 01:40.664
You had your hand up.

35
01:40.747 --> 01:43.500
You don't think I'm the right person for it either.

36
01:43.583 --> 01:44.584
I didn't.

37
01:45.168 --> 01:47.587
But the tables have turned.

38
01:49.548 --> 01:51.800
- What do you mean? - He was looking for you.

39
01:53.468 --> 01:54.678
The horizon.

40
01:54.761 --> 01:57.305
You went on and on and on about the horizon.

41
01:57.389 --> 02:00.183
Now that I finally found the person, what changed your mind?

42
02:00.267 --> 02:02.686
I'm not talking about the company. Let's just change the marketer.

43
02:02.769 --> 02:04.312
- What? - Instead of that woman

44
02:04.396 --> 02:06.982
bring me the person who came up with the horizon ad.

45
02:10.152 --> 02:11.611
Didn't I tell you?

46
02:11.695 --> 02:12.904
She's the one.

47
02:13.947 --> 02:16.491
- What? - So, be confident.

48
02:16.950 --> 02:19.536
You're not Gong Yeon-su from the blind date

49
02:19.619 --> 02:21.413
but Gong Yeon-su who created the horizon ad.

50
02:24.875 --> 02:27.502
Grapes for you.

51
02:27.794 --> 02:29.379
Mang-na. I knew I could count on you.

52
02:29.921 --> 02:33.216
Hey, don't you think calling me by my name

53
02:33.300 --> 02:35.093
when I'm 24 years older than you is a bit much?

54
02:35.177 --> 02:36.470
I don't mind hearing it though.

55
02:36.553 --> 02:39.222
I do it to any women who are older than me.

56
02:39.306 --> 02:41.433
I call every woman by their names except for my mom.

57
02:42.768 --> 02:44.686
You're really not prejudiced.

58
02:44.770 --> 02:47.689
You're the reason I come to work, to have fun with you.

59
02:51.568 --> 02:54.321
Excuse me.

60
03:13.799 --> 03:16.468
I'm sorry about last time.

61
03:16.551 --> 03:20.055
I don't normally drink that much. But that day...

62
03:22.098 --> 03:24.392
Anyway, I'm sorry about that.

63
03:24.476 --> 03:27.896
- It's okay. - And I'll pay you back

64
03:27.979 --> 03:32.025
- for your clothes. - Sure.

65
03:51.336 --> 03:54.506
Has it been decided that you'll be in charge of our product?

66
03:54.589 --> 03:57.509
- Yes, for now. - Let me ask a few questions.

67
03:57.592 --> 03:59.344
Have you ever used a sex toy before?

68
03:59.427 --> 04:02.055
- No. - Including our products?

69
04:03.181 --> 04:05.183
No, never.

70
04:05.267 --> 04:08.937
I didn't even know the name of your company until I received it.

71
04:09.354 --> 04:12.274
Is that a problem?

72
04:12.357 --> 04:14.985
Which part? Not knowing the name of our company?

73
04:15.068 --> 04:16.903
Or no sex toy experience?

74
04:17.195 --> 04:19.239
Being your blind date.

75
04:19.322 --> 04:22.450
- If that's what bugs you... - Yes.

76
04:23.326 --> 04:24.619
It bugs me.

77
04:24.703 --> 04:26.371
You being my blind date also bugs me.

78
04:26.454 --> 04:28.248
You've never used a sex toy before.

79
04:28.331 --> 04:30.333
And you didn't even know the name of our company.

80
04:31.251 --> 04:33.128
Just because I didn't know the name

81
04:33.211 --> 04:35.422
it doesn't mean I didn't know what this company does.

82
04:35.505 --> 04:37.674
Whether it's for a company or a product or an event

83
04:37.757 --> 04:39.676
the idea of marketing is the same.

84
04:39.843 --> 04:42.888
And it's my job to analyze and grasp

85
04:42.971 --> 04:44.764
- the target. - Is that so?

86
04:45.932 --> 04:47.684
Since you said so, let me ask you one more question.

87
04:49.519 --> 04:51.605
What do you think of sex toys?

88
04:54.858 --> 04:56.651
Do you have any intention of using them in the future?

89
05:01.072 --> 05:02.490
That answers my question.

90
05:02.574 --> 05:05.619
I can't leave it to a marketer who's biased about our product.

91
05:06.578 --> 05:08.163
I think we're done here.

92
05:08.246 --> 05:10.040
We're done here?

93
05:10.123 --> 05:11.541
Yes, we're done.

94
05:12.417 --> 05:13.418
You need to leave.

95
05:37.734 --> 05:41.529
Yes, I admit that I'm biased about your product.

96
05:41.863 --> 05:43.406
I don't know much about it

97
05:43.490 --> 05:45.659
and I never really paid attention to it.

98
05:46.201 --> 05:49.245
Honestly, it's true that I feel a bit resistant to it in some ways.

99
05:49.329 --> 05:50.455
But you know what?

100
05:50.622 --> 05:55.585
You'll find a lot of people like me in general.

101
05:55.669 --> 05:59.297
And they're your target in the end.

102
06:00.757 --> 06:06.012
Because I'm biased, I know how to overcome that bias.

103
06:10.850 --> 06:12.936
What does the horizon

104
06:13.436 --> 06:14.562
mean to you?

105
06:16.314 --> 06:17.440
The horizon ad.

106
06:18.441 --> 06:19.567
I heard it was your idea.

107
06:21.111 --> 06:22.570
I'm just curious about what that means.

108
06:22.988 --> 06:24.239
Well, it's just...

109
06:24.739 --> 06:26.950
a peaceful, safe

110
06:27.033 --> 06:29.494
- and stable life. - In detail.

111
06:32.414 --> 06:36.126
It's the line I keep my eyes on

112
06:37.210 --> 06:39.921
so I don't lose where I'm going.

113
06:40.505 --> 06:42.340
Sometimes I stop and look back to see

114
06:42.632 --> 06:48.888
if I've strayed from the path I wanted to take.

115
06:49.681 --> 06:50.849
It's the line

116
06:52.350 --> 06:53.727
that makes me start walking again.

117
06:53.977 --> 06:55.186
You mean like

118
06:56.021 --> 06:58.690
marriage?

119
07:03.069 --> 07:07.157
Well, I'm not sure whether it's a marriage or not.

120
07:07.657 --> 07:10.076
Because you can't guess how far the horizon is.

121
07:10.452 --> 07:14.998
I'm still walking toward it, but I haven't reached it yet.

122
07:16.624 --> 07:18.001
Does that answer your question?

123
07:21.337 --> 07:26.259
MAKE ME TINGLE

124
07:32.724 --> 07:34.726
Aunt Mi-young, it's not funny.

125
07:34.809 --> 07:36.352
No, I'm not saying it's funny.

126
07:37.687 --> 07:39.105
I'm proud of you.

127
07:40.065 --> 07:42.942
I knew people in this family

128
07:43.026 --> 07:46.362
tend to act first and think later. It runs in the family.

129
07:46.446 --> 07:49.824
I'm about to go crazy trying to do something crazy.

130
07:51.993 --> 07:53.995
What if I stray from the path

131
07:54.370 --> 07:56.706
- while trying a new one? - What's wrong with it?

132
07:57.332 --> 07:58.833
Just because you know it, doesn't mean you won't fall.

133
08:00.543 --> 08:03.588
Hey, life is no big deal. Don't think too much about it.

134
08:05.006 --> 08:06.299
Hey, it's burning. Flip it.

135
08:06.382 --> 08:07.926
- Flip it. - It's not burned.

136
08:08.009 --> 08:09.260
It is.

137
08:30.907 --> 08:34.619
It's the line I keep my eyes on

138
08:35.245 --> 08:38.039
so I don't lose where I'm going.

139
08:39.040 --> 08:43.753
I'm still walking toward it, but I haven't reached it yet.

140
09:02.397 --> 09:04.440
We finally have...

141
09:04.524 --> 09:06.359
A new girl.

142
09:18.371 --> 09:19.789
The vice president is late.

143
09:20.874 --> 09:23.877
Sorry. It was hard to put on the butt-lifting shapewear today.

144
09:28.923 --> 09:30.300
His boyfriend?

145
09:30.633 --> 09:32.802
Say hi. He's our vice president.

146
09:33.511 --> 09:35.680
Gong Yeon-su, right? I'm Yun Ji-o.

147
09:35.763 --> 09:38.016
Oh, yes. Hello.

148
09:38.099 --> 09:40.685
This is Ma Mang-na, the product designer.

149
09:40.768 --> 09:42.437
He's Joo Min-hyung, the web designer.

150
09:42.604 --> 09:43.771
Nice to meet you.

151
09:44.731 --> 09:47.609
Finally, I'm not the only woman here anymore.

152
09:48.401 --> 09:50.904
Can I call you by your name when the bosses aren't here?

153
09:51.905 --> 09:53.948
I'm Gong Yeon-su from SR Marketing Group.

154
09:54.032 --> 09:56.034
I'll be in charge of promoting your new release.

155
09:56.117 --> 09:59.704
I look forward to working with you.

156
09:59.787 --> 10:01.372
You can call me

157
10:01.581 --> 10:04.000
Ms. Gong.

158
10:04.626 --> 10:07.378
The vice president will tell you about the rest.

159
10:07.503 --> 10:09.214
- Sure. - You're dismissed.

160
10:09.464 --> 10:11.257
Oh, Mr. Dokgo. You need to look at this.

161
10:11.925 --> 10:13.593
This too.

162
10:15.386 --> 10:16.763
Here.

163
10:17.096 --> 10:19.224
- Is this my desk? - Now

164
10:19.515 --> 10:20.892
do you want me to show you around?

165
10:23.853 --> 10:26.481
You said you'd show me around.

166
10:26.564 --> 10:28.900
Yes, it's the in-company cafe.

167
10:29.400 --> 10:31.069
This place has good coffee.

168
10:38.910 --> 10:40.703
Dal told me.

169
10:40.787 --> 10:42.455
You met on a blind date?

170
10:43.539 --> 10:45.667
Don't take it wrong.

171
10:45.750 --> 10:48.211
The blind date has nothing to do with this...

172
10:48.294 --> 10:51.381
I know. Dal seeing a woman on a blind date

173
10:51.464 --> 10:53.049
of all people?

174
10:54.259 --> 10:57.345
My boss is actually pretty blunt and prickly.

175
10:57.595 --> 11:00.598
Still, he means no harm. So don't take it personally.

176
11:00.682 --> 11:01.933
That's what I wanted to tell you.

177
11:02.642 --> 11:04.435
Yes, I'll do my best.

178
11:05.186 --> 11:07.647
Doing my best is my specialty.

179
11:09.315 --> 11:10.692
Still

180
11:10.858 --> 11:13.569
I'm new to this field.

181
11:13.736 --> 11:15.613
I'm going to need your help.

182
11:15.697 --> 11:16.990
Of course.

183
11:17.073 --> 11:18.574
Feel free to ask me.

184
11:18.658 --> 11:19.909
I'll be here to help you.

185
11:20.743 --> 11:23.496
But don't tell Dal.

186
11:23.579 --> 11:26.165
Does it have to be a secret?

187
11:26.249 --> 11:27.750
He won't say anything good anyway.

188
11:27.834 --> 11:29.669
From what I know...

189
11:30.837 --> 11:33.214
Mind your own business.

190
11:39.053 --> 11:40.471
You guys look pretty close.

191
11:41.723 --> 11:43.641
Whatever. I hate you.

192
11:43.725 --> 11:45.727
Honey, don't be upset.

193
11:49.439 --> 11:51.149
Still...

194
11:51.232 --> 11:53.818
Now, let's talk about the tuition.

195
11:53.901 --> 11:55.570
- The tuition? - I'm not asking for much.

196
11:55.653 --> 11:57.822
A cup of coffee from time to time will do.

197
11:57.905 --> 12:00.783
Well, sure.

198
12:00.867 --> 12:03.578
Oh, right. That means you need money.

199
12:05.121 --> 12:07.081
- Ta-da. - My wallet.

200
12:07.373 --> 12:08.791
- How do you have this? - Well...

201
12:09.584 --> 12:11.169
I found it in front of the club.

202
12:11.252 --> 12:12.962
Oh, thank you so much.

203
12:13.296 --> 12:16.007
I reported everything lost.

204
12:16.090 --> 12:17.675
You owe me one.

205
12:17.884 --> 12:20.470
- Now, are you ready for a real tour? - Yes.

206
12:29.020 --> 12:31.689
This is where we try the products.

207
12:31.773 --> 12:32.857
What?

208
12:33.399 --> 12:34.817
In the company?

209
12:34.901 --> 12:37.236
- Yes. Something wrong? - But...

210
12:38.905 --> 12:41.157
- During work? - It is work.

211
12:41.240 --> 12:42.408
It's part of our job.

212
12:44.160 --> 12:46.579
You're free to use it anytime.

213
12:46.913 --> 12:48.456
Oh, don't forget to lock the door.

214
12:49.040 --> 12:52.168
No, I'm good.

215
12:56.381 --> 12:58.758
- Are you using it? - No.

216
13:01.177 --> 13:03.054
This is the Development Room

217
13:03.137 --> 13:05.014
where we design and engineer everything.

218
13:05.723 --> 13:07.809
After the prototypes are made at the factory

219
13:07.892 --> 13:09.685
we test and improve them here.

220
13:09.769 --> 13:13.064
This is where you can see the entire history of Loand.

221
13:21.239 --> 13:23.449
All right. Here's a test.

222
13:24.033 --> 13:28.204
- Guess what this is. - Is that also a toy?

223
13:28.579 --> 13:30.123
It looks like a tumbler, doesn't it?

224
13:30.665 --> 13:34.877
We have ones that look like eggs and muffins.

225
13:35.586 --> 13:38.798
Our ancestors used animals' horns or wood.

226
13:38.881 --> 13:42.677
Guess when the oldest sex toy in human history was made.

227
13:44.679 --> 13:47.682
- I'm not sure. - It was 30,000 years ago.

228
13:47.765 --> 13:50.560
This world has history too.

229
13:51.060 --> 13:52.061
Of course.

230
13:53.938 --> 13:55.356
Cleopatra

231
13:55.565 --> 13:57.733
put a bunch of bees inside a gourd

232
13:57.817 --> 13:59.485
and made it vibrate artificially.

233
13:59.902 --> 14:02.155
Cleopatra. Wow.

234
14:11.372 --> 14:15.334
- And here's your homework. - For me?

235
14:18.254 --> 14:20.131
What is this?

236
14:20.214 --> 14:23.885
Think about why mankind created things like this.

237
14:23.968 --> 14:25.303
Think about it?

238
14:27.263 --> 14:28.306
Okay.

239
15:07.970 --> 15:10.598
Be good. Stay quiet.

240
15:17.104 --> 15:20.608
Yusecha

241
15:20.691 --> 15:26.197
Eolsachirwol gapjasang

242
15:26.447 --> 15:29.283
So? Is your crazy thing worth doing?

243
15:30.660 --> 15:32.286
I'm getting used to it.

244
15:33.454 --> 15:34.705
By any chance

245
15:35.581 --> 15:37.750
are you bringing any toys home?

246
15:39.585 --> 15:40.586
Are you crazy?

247
15:43.548 --> 15:45.049
How can I bring them home?

248
15:45.132 --> 15:46.634
Hey. You brought coffee home all the time

249
15:46.717 --> 15:49.053
when you were working on the coffee ad.

250
15:49.679 --> 15:50.888
Hush.

251
15:53.307 --> 15:56.561
Chuwongamsi

252
15:56.811 --> 16:00.106
Bulseongyeongmo

253
16:00.189 --> 16:03.109
Geuni

254
16:03.192 --> 16:06.112
Jeongjakseosu

255
16:06.487 --> 16:07.655
It's not me.

256
16:10.992 --> 16:12.785
Seriously, Nam-su...

257
16:21.544 --> 16:23.379
Wait!

258
16:24.422 --> 16:25.798
What's going on?

259
16:25.881 --> 16:28.426
- What's wrong? - Uncle.

260
16:28.634 --> 16:29.885
Wait.

261
16:30.678 --> 16:33.306
Please let it go.

262
16:33.389 --> 16:34.765
Turn your phone off during the memorial ceremony.

263
16:34.849 --> 16:36.934
Yes, I'll turn it off.

264
16:37.018 --> 16:38.519
No, I'll do it.

265
16:54.035 --> 16:56.412
I'm doomed.

266
16:57.538 --> 16:59.040
Wait!

267
16:59.123 --> 17:01.876
Oh, my goodness.

268
17:03.586 --> 17:06.047
Stop her.

269
17:28.069 --> 17:31.656
Gong Yeon-su, I told you not to touch my stuff.

270
17:31.739 --> 17:32.865
What?

271
17:33.157 --> 17:35.660
I know you're tired from working overtime

272
17:36.202 --> 17:38.079
but why did you take my massager?

273
17:39.080 --> 17:40.581
Oh, no.

274
17:40.665 --> 17:43.417
Is that a massager?

275
17:44.460 --> 17:47.171
If it's not a massager, what would it be?

276
17:48.005 --> 17:49.965
It spins

277
17:50.466 --> 17:55.137
and massages your traps.

278
17:55.221 --> 17:56.972
I can't take this anymore.

279
17:57.056 --> 17:59.642
- Good grief. - How dare you make a fuss

280
17:59.850 --> 18:01.143
on the day of a memorial ceremony?

281
18:01.644 --> 18:02.770
Especially during the first day of his burial!

282
18:02.853 --> 18:04.105
Get out of here.

283
18:04.480 --> 18:05.564
Now!

284
18:17.868 --> 18:20.830
If you're going to act up again during the memorial ceremony

285
18:20.913 --> 18:22.373
stay outside.

286
18:22.456 --> 18:24.208
Where can I go?

287
18:24.291 --> 18:25.668
It's always held late at night.

288
18:25.751 --> 18:27.086
I have no place to go.

289
18:27.169 --> 18:30.089
So why did you get divorced?

290
18:30.381 --> 18:34.385
Why are you bringing that up now?

291
18:34.719 --> 18:36.137
That's enough.

292
18:37.346 --> 18:39.181
Buy ham.

293
18:39.265 --> 18:41.434
Buy ham.

294
18:41.517 --> 18:43.352
Buy ham.

295
18:43.436 --> 18:46.605
- Buy ham. - It's cold. Hurry up and get inside.

296
18:47.231 --> 18:49.358
How much is in there?

297
18:49.900 --> 18:51.652
It's not enough to move my legs.

298
18:51.736 --> 18:54.572
Oh, it's cold. Hurry up and come inside.

299
18:56.574 --> 19:00.202
My aunt, who had a passionate romance but had an arranged marriage

300
19:00.286 --> 19:02.747
said she had never been happy even for a moment.

301
19:03.622 --> 19:06.041
When I asked her why she was getting married

302
19:06.292 --> 19:07.710
she said...

303
19:08.419 --> 19:09.587
Well...

304
19:10.755 --> 19:11.839
Because...

305
19:14.008 --> 19:15.593
I feel like this is the right thing to do.

306
19:24.351 --> 19:26.812
KOREAN HISTORY

307
19:39.492 --> 19:40.493
Nam-su.

308
19:43.788 --> 19:47.541
Nam-su couldn't disobey the family simply because he was a son.

309
19:50.169 --> 19:53.464
So he's been forced to drink herbal medicine

310
19:53.547 --> 19:55.466
